 🎓 Breaking: Citadel founder and CEO Ken Griffin is making a $3 billion donation to Carnegie Mellon University, which calls it "the largest-ever gift by an individual in the history of higher education."

 $1 billion will bolster CMU's historic Pittsburgh campus. $2 billion will fund the launch of Carnegie Mellon University Miami , "designed to pioneer a model for higher education ... for the next era of American innovation." CMU Miami's 35-acre campus in the Wynwood neighborhood aims to open in 2028. Read the announcement ... Griffin's giving . 
 
