 3. 🇮🇷 Hope fades on Iran talks 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Jared Kushner and Vice President Vance in Switzerland in June, with Qatari mediator Ali al-Thawadi in the foreground. Photo: Nathan Howard-Pool/Getty Images Efforts this week by Qatari mediators to broker a diplomatic breakthrough between the U.S. and Iran have made little progress, with neither side willing to budge, three sources familiar with the talks tell Axios' Barak Ravid. 

 "It is stuck," one of the sources said. "The Iranians are asking for things the U.S. can't accept. And the U.S. thinks it is winning so there is no need for compromise." Why it matters: The stalemate bolsters the belief on both sides that a renewed military conflict is becoming more likely. 

 💣 U.S. officials think President Trump could order a return to major combat operations after the midterms.

 Qatari officials will keep trying but are growing increasingly frustrated with both sides, two of the sources said. More on the talks . 

 
 
