 5. 📈 Surprise stat: Media trust rebounds slightly 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Gallup . Chart: Axios Visuals For the first time in years,  trust in media rebounded slightly among Americans — a 5-point gain after an 8-year slide,  Axios Media Trends expert Sara Fischer writes. 

 Why it matters: The trend is driven by a bounce in trust among Republicans. Gallup didn't speculate about why. A wide partisan gap remains: A mere 22% of Republicans trust the press vs. half of Dems. By the numbers: Around one-third of Americans (33%) say they have a great deal or a fair amount of trust in mass media, according to a new Gallup survey — up from 28% last year, a record low.

 Republicans' trust sharply rebounded from 8% last year to 22% today. Democrats' trust stayed statistically flat at 50%. 😬 Reality check: "Despite this year's increase, confidence in the media remains near the bottom of Gallup's more than 50-year trend."

