 8. 🎒 Heftiest bear crowned 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A brown bear known as Backpack, officially named Bear 89, wades through Brooks River in Katmai National Park &amp; Preserve in Alaska on Sept. 8. Image from video: explore.org via AP Backpack — "Lord of Lard, Earl of Girth" — won the 12th annual Fat Bear Week, officially declared the heftiest bear in Alaska's Katmai National Park &amp; Preserve.

 20 years old and packing an estimated 1,000-1,200 pounds, Backpack prevailed from a bracket of 16 chunky bears after a week of online voting . He pulled in more than 100,000 votes in the final round. The competition celebrates the resilience of 2,200 brown bears living in the Alaska Peninsula preserve. Bear 910 stands beside the Brooks River in Alaska on Sept. 9. Photo: C. Loberg/National Park Service via AP Above, the runner-up: Bear 910, the daughter of a former champion.

